asizes pricing power, supply scarcity, and execution discipline; avoids overpromising on timelines but signals strong momentum; tone reflects control over narrative and market position.","src":"concall","title":"Management quality / tone"},{"body":"Buyers are purchasing 2-3 units to create 12,000-15,000 sq.ft duplexes — indicating ultra-high-net-worth demand and asset consolidation behavior, not just housing needs; SRA redevelopment success without intermediaries is a rare competitive moat in Mumbai.","src":"concall","title":"Non-obvious takeaways"},{"body":"- Maintains a conservative balance sheet with low leverage to support growth and withstand market cycles.\n- Consistent dividend payout track record reflecting commitment to shareholder returns.","src":"deck","title":"Capital allocation policy (investor deck)"}],"business":[{"body":"Residential: 360 West (Worli) sold 77/200 units at ₹1.0-1.1 Cr/sq.ft RERA carpet; Goregaon/Borivali sold out Towers A/B; Mulund pricing up 5-10%; Retail: Borivali Mall pre-COVID consumption restored; Commercial: Commerz III nearing completion with strong tenant interest; Redevelopment: SRA site adjacent to Sky City cleared, 95% vacated.","src":"concall","title":"Segment / subsidiary detail"},{"body":"> Only challenges the company specifically discussed on this call. Names resolved against our own companies/products files + StockMetadata. ✅=covered here, ⭐=sector-knowledge.\n\n| Challenge (their words) | Beneficiary — NSE · BSE | Loser — NSE · BSE | Why / conviction |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Eco Sensitive Zone/Supreme Court order halted construction activity near fault lines in MMR; caused delay to Thane (Kolshet/Pokhran) and Borivali launches | — | SUNTECK REALTY LIMITED — SUNTECK · 512179 | Oberoi says Eco Sensitive Zone/court order delayed Thane launch; all MMR developers with greenfield Thane/peripheral MMR land similarly impacted by the same regulatory bottleneck in Q2FY23 / Low |\n| Input material costs have gone up - steel is a key construction input; company forced to raise prices 5-10% across projects | JSW STEEL LIMITED — JSWSTEEL · 500228 | — | Material cost pressure cited broadly; steel is key construction input; JSW is largest listed steel producer with domestic pricing power in a cost-up cycle / Med |\n| Input material costs have gone up - steel, cement and other construction materials; company forced to raise prices 5-10% across projects | ULTRATECH CEMENT LIMITED — ULTRACEMCO · 532538 | — | Vikas Oberoi explicitly cites material costs up; cement is largest construction input; UltraTech as market leader passes through price hikes / High |\n| Interest costs going up for developers - cited as a significant headwind alongside input costs, squeezing leveraged developers who cannot raise prices | LIC HOUSING FINANCE LTD — LICHSGFIN · 500253 | — | Oberoi states interest costs risen for developers; HFCs and NBFCs lending to developers earn higher yields in rising rate environment, though asset quality risk also rises for weaker borrowers / Low |\n| Lack of credible suppliers - Oberoi explicitly cites this as enabling premium demand and minimal competition, particularly for ready-to-move Worli inventory | OBEROI REALTY LIMITED — OBEROIRLTY · 533273 | — | Self-referential but directly stated: Oberoi says residential business outperforms due to \"robust demand and lack of credible suppliers\" - they are the supply side scarcity play / High |\n| Manpower costs going up - cited explicitly alongside material and approval costs as reasons for price hikes across all projects | TEAMLEASE SERVICES LTD. — TEAMLEASE · 539658 | — | Vikas Oberoi explicitly says manpower costs up; TeamLease as leading construction/general workforce staffing player benefits from tighter labour markets and higher bill rates / Med |\n| Rising input and interest costs threatening delivery viability of smaller/weaker developers - Oberoi says he fears other developers cannot deliver if they do not raise prices | — | LODHA DEVELOPERS LIMITED — LODHA · 543287 | Oberoi says smaller/less credible developers face delivery risk given cost surge; Lodha (then recently listed) carried high leverage and similar MMR exposure, making it representative of this risk / Low |","src":"concall","title":"Challenges → beneficiaries & losers (listed names)"},{"body":"- Focus on premium residential, commercial, retail, and hospitality segments in the Mumbai Metropolitan Region.\n- Emphasizes brand reputation, design quality, and timely delivery as key differentiators.","src":"deck","title":"Positioning (investor deck)"}],"latest_quarter":[{"body":"rev: +45% YoY; EBITDA: +52% YoY; PAT: +68% YoY; orderbook: ₹12,500 Cr; netdebt: ₹1,800 Cr (net cash positive)","src":"concall","title":"Financial scorecard"},{"body":"Residential margins expanding due to pricing power (Worli realization up 50% YoY); input costs up 15-20% (labor, materials, approvals); 5-10% price hikes implemented across projects since Oct 2022; commercial margins expected to be 35%+ post-completion.","src":"concall","title":"Margins & cost dynamics"}],"outlook":[{"body":"Launches planned in Thane, Borivali, and Goregaon within Q3FY23; Glaxo land use decision (residential vs. commercial) expected by end of Q3FY23; no formal guidance issued beyond near-term launches.","src":"concall","title":"Guidance"},{"body":"₹12,500 Cr (including ₹8,500 Cr from Worli 360 West unsold inventory and ₹4,000 Cr from other projects)","src":"concall","title":"Order book & pipeline"},{"body":"Glaxo land parcel (10+ acres) for commercial/mall or residential; redevelopment pipeline in Mumbai (multiple projects in advanced talks); potential for 1M sq.ft commercial expansion in Borivali/Sky City corridor; expansion beyond MMR under evaluation.","src":"concall","title":"Growth verticals / optionality"}]},"sources":["Q2FY23 concall summary","structured quarterly financials","investor presentation (08-05-2026)","credit-rating action (CARE ESG Ratings Limited 27-06-2026)"],"thes